b.concept('compute_algebra','Typed compute C algebra','Language validation boundary intended to keep LLM-authored canonical declaration data within GTL/HoG/ABG structure through published APIs and typed repair, without reliance on remembered prose distinctions.',[(14,12,19)])
b.concept('gtl_requirement_domain','GTL language-law domain','GTL 3 constitutional language and graph-law domain for an LLM-first, graph-first algebraic governance control language with implementation-independent canonical declaration data and native typed APIs in each conforming tenant.',[(4,3,7)])
b.constraint('tuner_read_boundary',['reflective_tuner','tuner_observations'],'The tuner reads only the listed replay-derived models; it must neither maintain a second truth store nor consume unattributed telemetry.',[(0,31,31)])
b.constraint('tuner_public_relations',['reflective_tuner'],'All tuner acts project through exactly two accepted public relation identities. tune report binds pure abg.operation.project.read and emits no event or mutation; tune propose, ratify and reject are variants of abg.operation.tuning.transition entering ordinary admitted actor or policy truth. Command spellings are not operation identities.',[(0,33,40)])
b.constraint('tuner_write_and_judgment_separation',['reflective_tuner','tuning_draft'],'Tuner output is declaration drafts only, never live declarations, code, workspace assets or runtime state. Ratified drafts re-enter ordinary admitted work via the owning ticket and change class. Solve writes candidates, optimize writes terms; no program performs both in one judgment. Optimization may not diagnose or triage defects; observer/tuner truth exchange occurs only via admitted intake or telemetry records, never within one judgment.',[(0,42,42)])
b.constraint('draft_ratification_gate',['tuning_draft'],'Preserve all typed draft-state and provenance fields. Human F_H ratification is the default; auto-ratification is lawful only under declared visible policy, never by omission.',[(0,44,44)],exceptions=['Declared visible policy may authorize automatic ratification.'])
b.constraint('annealing_equivalence',['reflective_tuner','tuning_draft'],'An F_D-specific interior may replace a typed F_P generic only through an admitted annealing proposal carrying an admitted equivalence contract. Hand-tuned F_D interiors are unlawful; telemetry-derived tuner output supplies local-loop tightening. Equivalence preserves outer identity, declared obligations, evidence classes and replay comparability. Post-ratification divergence becomes a typed defect routed to intake and reprice, including lawful demotion to the F_P generic.',[(0,46,48)],conditions=['Replacement of an F_P generic by an F_D-specific interior.'])
b.constraint('tuner_calibration_and_crystallization',['reflective_tuner','tuning_draft'],'Evaluator calibration concerning retry burn, contract-shape variance, ambiguity pressure or prompt/instruction categories derives from telemetry and follows draft/ratify. Tuner crystallization includes lay-rail publication when per-contract composition entropy is near zero, pull-up retirement of non-discriminating edges, and abstraction naming of proven compositions as catalog graph functions. Catalog visibility curation also follows the same draft ratification gate.',[(0,50,52),(0,58,58)])
b.constraint('tuner_typed_signals',['reflective_tuner','tuner_observations'],'Mode/track observables are typed and replay-derived and include at minimum route variance/composition entropy, retry density, repeated path shape, per-contract cost, closure rate, adapter-gap counts and defect recurrence. A declared path halting on ambiguity projects a rail-break mode-selection signal before same-edge retry burn. Promotion/demotion drafts cite admitted signal rows by reference; F_P interpretation is a proposal, and narrative labels supply no authority.',[(0,54,54)])
b.constraint('candidate_family_mode_choice',['reflective_tuner','tuning_draft'],'Declared and emergent interiors are two CandidateFamily alternatives over one outer contract under visible policy. Tuner promotion/demotion drafts move contracts between modes, while actual selection remains lawful selection of published alternatives.',[(0,56,56)])
b.constraint('tuner_closure_proof',['reflective_tuner'],'Before claiming runtime/live closure, deterministic tests must cover report non-append, draft admission and ratified/rejected states, human versus policy auto-ratification, rejection of annealing without equivalence, divergence intake/demotion, lay-rail/pull-up/abstraction shapes on entropy fixtures, rail-break projection, rejection without admitted signal references, rejection of triage output from tuning judgments, and prohibition of every live-surface mutation path. Event kinds initiating, terminating, clipping or declipping runtime fluents require declared Event Calculus effects before implementation closure. Draft states and entropy projections remain replay-derived, not primary event authority.',[(0,60,62)])
b.latitude('tuner_extension_latitude',['reflective_tuner'],['Override the default tuning loop through declared hook/policy surfaces.','F_P may propose interpretation of admitted typed signals.'],['Adding runner mechanics or kernel particle classes.','Treating narrative mode labels as authority.'],[(0,29,29),(0,54,54)])
b.relation('tuner_consumes_replay','reads_only','reflective_tuner','tuner_observations','The tuner receives its entire read basis from replay-derived read models.',[(0,31,31)],True)
b.relation('tuner_produces_drafts','writes_only','reflective_tuner','tuning_draft','The only tuner write product is a declaration draft which must pass ratification and ordinary work admission before effects.',[(0,42,44)],True)
b.constraint('worker_binding_admission',['worker'],'GTL declares role requirements; Product or implementation-binding resolution may propose a match, and ABG must admit or reject it before HoG traversal and realization of selected leaf effects. ABG consumes externally resolved identity and does not implement authentication; when provided it preserves external authority references or equivalent hooks. build/build_id reporting metadata cannot substitute for identity.',[(3,20,26)],conditions=['Preserve external authority references or hooks when provided.'])
b.constraint('worker_concurrency_boundary',['worker'],'Worker capability exposes write territory sufficiently for declared policy to propose concurrency, ABG to admit/reject the safety basis, HoG to apply only admitted disposition, and implementation bindings to realize only those leaf effects. Parallel GTL worker/job branches require an ABG-admitted proof of disjoint write territories. Overlapping writes produce a serial policy proposal subject to the same admission/traversal/effect chain; read overlap alone is not a conflict.',[(3,28,32)],conditions=['Parallel traversal requires admitted proof of disjoint writes.'],exceptions=['Read overlap alone does not prohibit parallelism.'])
b.constraint('asset_surface_subordination',['asset_surface'],'AssetSurface remains subordinate declaration truth, not a new topology object, public execution target or GraphFunction/Job rival. Preserve kind, requiredContexts, standardsRefs and outputContractRefs, and preserve the full interface without semantic loss across constructor, admission, serialization, module publication and graph-function chain composition.',[(9,19,21),(9,39,39)])
b.latitude('asset_surface_optional_interfaces',['asset_surface'],['Declare typed constructor references and input asset kinds, renderer references, view-digest policy and proof-obligation references.','Renderer-backed surfaces may declare section/clause kinds only as rendered-view metadata.','Prompt-like or renderer-backed surfaces may declare generic authority slots.','Deterministic consumers may check declared metadata, schemas, references, digest policy, authority-slot and fallback-policy shape.'],['Creating a new language ontology from section/clause kinds.','Inferring prompt-clause, asset-obligation or behavior semantics from rendered text.'],[(9,23,27),(9,37,37)])
b.constraint('asset_authority_slot_law',['asset_surface'],'Each declared authority slot carries an opaque authority-kind reference and exactly a normal, bounded_fallback or forbidden_routine disposition. GTL owns slot shape/labels; downstream Products own authority vocabulary and assignment policy. Every bounded_fallback slot requires at least one precondition reference checked by GTL admission. ABG/downstream assurance determines lawful concrete runtime use. forbidden_routine slots survive publication, admission and serialization for deterministic policy enforcement without text inference.',[(9,27,31)],conditions=['A slot is declared.','At least one fallback precondition reference is required for each bounded_fallback slot.'])
b.constraint('asset_admission_and_view_boundary',['asset_surface'],'Declaration admission validates metadata shape only: references, dispositions, fallback presence, constructor/renderer and proof references; it cannot decide Product vocabulary, accepted prompt content or runtime-packet legality. Derived rendered text, markdown, terminal output and UI views never outrank typed declarations, constructors, authority slots or proofs.',[(9,33,35)])
b.constraint('observer_asset_context',['asset_surface'],'Executive-observer asset surfaces bind target-workspace availability through existing requiredContexts and proof-obligation references. They create neither an observer asset ontology nor authoritative rendered workspace summaries over typed context, payload, evidence, span-lineage and projection references.',[(9,41,45)],conditions=['The asset surface is used by the ABG executive observer.'])
b.constraint('attrs_carriage',['attrs'],'Attrs preserves stable ordered key/value truth and fails closed on duplicates. It must be usable at minimum on Rule.config, GraphFunction.declarations, GraphVector.declarations, RefinementBoundary.hints, CandidateFamily.policy_hints, Job.policy_hooks, Role.policy_hooks, Module.policy_hooks and Module.metadata; it remains inspectable, serializable and replayable across publication/interpretation.',[(12,21,25)])
b.constraint('compute_sort_chain',['compute_algebra'],'The declared chain is Module/catalog to GraphFunction<A,B>, GraphFunction to internal GraphVector<A,B>, the pair to declared C<A,B>, C to CStage<Role,Fibre,X,Y>, and CStage to admitted implementation of the same role/fibre/type boundary. GraphFunction, GraphVector, program/overlay, workspace, C, stage, fibre, implementation binding, TraversalUnit and runtime state stay distinct sorts. Only a named constructor creates a conversion; structural resemblance, observed behavior, execution count and downstream terminology never coerce sorts.',[(15,23,37)])
b.constraint('gtl_domain_scope',['gtl_requirement_domain'],'The language domain covers declaration and engine boundaries, typed graph structures and identities, asset interfaces, operators/evaluators/rules/hooks, graph functions/selection/synthesis/subwork, composition/substitution/recursion/higher order operations, semantic work/module publication and requirement wrappers. Epistemic notation distinguishes candidates, findings, admission, runtime/projection ledgers and consequences without new topology/runtime carriers. Product-visible graph programs are validated as GTL, traversed by HoG and admitted by ABG.',[(5,25,42)])
